    "frame_count": 15,
    "frame_rate": 4,
    "g00_zero_meaning": "g_00 = 0 is where the coordinate vector d/dt becomes null: an ergosurface-type condition on the TIME COORDINATE. It is not a metric degeneracy, not a signature failure, not a curvature singularity and not automatically a horizon. det(g) and the spatial metric remain regular there and the ADM foliation persists.",
    "git_commit": "77b4617a216d1b72e7d71edebeb6da92d8b12259",
    "git_dirty": true,
    "milestone": "A6",
    "numerical_error_envelope_floor": 0.0004,
    "observer_admissibility": "The coordinate-stationary observer is admissible ONLY where g_00 < 0. At g_00 = 0 the coordinate vector d/dt is NULL and for g_00 > 0 it is SPACELIKE; in both cases it is rejected with a reason and its energy-density cell is left EMPTY. |g_00| is never substituted. The Eulerian observer is built from the ADM normal and remains timelike through the crossing; it is recorded separately.",
    "observer_families": [
